      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree eff2de574be8461e4fcda1397514e9585a292efd\nparent 2063f02bd5edebe1b5c9635db8850220811ebc90\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1783027311 -0700\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1783312715 -0700\n\ntxdb: reject malformed first coin cursor key\n\n`CCoinsViewDB::Cursor()` already handles an empty coin keyspace after `Seek(DB_COIN)`, but could still accept an undecodable first coin key as a valid cursor position.\n`CCoinsViewDBCursor::Next()` invalidates the cursor for the same decode failure later in iteration, so the warmup path had a small malformed-chainstate consistency gap.\n\nMake initial cursor setup match `Next()`: keep the cached key invalid unless the first key decodes successfully.\nAdd a unit test that writes a valid `Coin` under a malformed `DB_COIN` key and checks the cursor is invalid.\n\nCo-authored-by: Shuvam Pandey <i@shuvamp.com.np>\nCo-authored-by: Arthur Ariel Sabintsev <arthur@sabintsev.com>\nCo-authored-by: CruzMolina <7537712+CruzMolina@users.noreply.github.com>\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEqXy8dDLWkKQdUrTAZp//D/pHenYFAmpLMUsACgkQZp//D/pH\nenZnoQ/+PktlSLzxGNyfhhtsuq8dApoC5FBpaBDra6BDhlIImVg6mXLkuO+JV/qo\nnn/wW2nHJV78zJcefWaGSGFDitWunAO1fwgFA303/BwagG8k2k4ItU5rl3KVwqfG\nswSD3pRoPhQV71ht3iF8viFRUv7caDLRN9UeJmN2G9l/NmZl4jYu/xVcJkCgboAH\nuFeryfqwesYLLkFPLMC6XAx7r2jcns2P7oDRqOTmZPdxNnls3ahrzSQsqhsVfwyH\n5gM7LBGIGUBH1bYJ6NnGFhns7P33qXpIseyqU7hJQ9Lsp1Sy0B9Ju+QvwZ+jfS1C\numZVtWH2i4CUxTH1H6CHN6w/YTP2+qbRw5cQ2nlsvba2vPnKar23lT12DJvnd+hY\nPkMo9fWJooj4fMJdbZFMa0nMJILbpKNL/VuV9u4BrxMMth45Agnosfmy0ZLGzvPj\nvLCmI/0DpNluKiMKlyWnrXq6pzNoBtMp21BNxZ4hTjKoYW8RV8uUCiadoAw5OfU5\nOr36XHFnKj8UIR7HrRl0Hl35xNFZFKbpwTvbszZYSsfW/8jU9FKEGstWUuci1K1C\nOCKfOOuA/2FJ5ykpBK4cdsLsxLHWbh4YraoFbDHHO8QNBJpJZYCaAGX1j19x0PuP\nt3JtsotALkrZfjrwe36+8kPw4X9wWjq6H5D6VZ3V9K8bwgLl8oA=\n=yECV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
